---
// Terms and conditions. Live content here is not the site's terms at all:
// it is a standalone 2018 event page for a Wellington Dam "conservation
// zone" plot sale, kept live at this URL ever since (see
// docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-live-site-rebuild.md §2, which flags it
// for client review). Carried rather than rewritten, since the client owns
// the decision on what belongs at this URL long term.
//
// The customer waiver PDF link on live (181127-customer-waiver-for-
// conservation-zone) resolves with a 301 to a real PDF; downloaded to
// public/documents/customer-waiver-for-conservation-zone.pdf and linked
// directly rather than through the old redirect.
//
// The terms themselves are now real text, transcribed word for word from
// that PDF (Waiver & Release, and the memorial tree terms and warranty), so
// they can be read on a phone, by screen readers and by search engines.
// Wording, spelling and capitals are exactly as the PDF has them, including
// its known slips (clause 2 of the waiver ends mid-sentence; "Cancellations
// made at within 21 from purchase"); fixing them is the client's call. The
// PDF's blank form fields and signature line are left to the PDF itself.
//
// The event label and the "Purchase your plot" button were removed at the
// client's request; the waiver download is the page's one action.
//
// Dropped as noise rather than content: live repeats the waiver PDF link
// and the "Purchase your plot" button a second time each further down the
// page, an about:blank map iframe with nothing to embed, a Facebook/
// Twitter/LinkedIn share widget with no working share targets without its
// original plugin, and a page-specific 2018 mini footer (address,
// copyright, social links) that would sit directly above this site's real,
// current footer and only contradict it.
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BlogToc from '@/components/blog/BlogToc.astro';
import Prose from '@/components/Prose.astro';
import { buttonVariants } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { Separator } from '@/components/ui/separator';

const title = 'Terms and conditions';
const description =
  'Terms and conditions and the customer waiver for the Wellington Dam Memorial Forest conservation zone.';

const WAIVER_PDF_HREF = '/documents/customer-waiver-for-conservation-zone.pdf';

// The document's sections, for the contents list. Ids match the h2s below.
const headings = [
  { id: 'waiver-and-release', text: 'Waiver & Release' },
  { id: 'terms-and-warranty', text: 'Living Legacy Memorial Tree terms & warranty' },
  { id: 'cancellations-and-refunds', text: 'Cancellations & Refunds' },
  { id: 'planted-living-legacy-trees', text: 'Planted LIVING LEGACY TREES' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 sm:px-10 lg:py-28">
    <header class="rise-children max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display-title mt-4">Terms and conditions</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-6">
        All customers must agree to the standard terms and conditions and waiver to take part in
        this memorial sanctuary event. By purchasing your plot you agree to be bound by these terms
        and conditions.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href={WAIVER_PDF_HREF}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class={buttonVariants()}
        >
          Customer waiver PDF download
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Contents beside the terms from lg, as on the privacy policy; a
         collapsible panel above them on smaller screens. -->
    <div class="mt-14 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[12rem_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:items-start lg:gap-16">
      <div class="hidden lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:block">
        <BlogToc headings={headings} label="On this page" />
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <BlogToc
          headings={headings}
          label="On this page"
          variant="collapsible"
          class="mb-10 lg:hidden"
        />
        <Prose>
          <p>Living Legacy Standard Terms and Conditions 2016 Ver 1.0</p>

          <h2 id="waiver-and-release">Waiver &amp; Release</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>
              I desire to participate voluntarily in the planting and memorial activities
              facilitated by Living Legacy Forest Pty Ltd (“LLT”) on the SITE.
            </li>
            <li>
              I understand, accept, and assume the risks associated with participation in any and
              all activities relating to the planting day and accessing the conservation site. I
              also assume the responsibility of conducting myself in a civil manner that is mutually
              beneficial to all participants. Unacceptable conduct generally includes, but is not
              limited to theft, profanity, causing damage whether intentionally or recklessly and
              any offensive behaviour. I agree and understand that I should wear suitable clothes
              and shoes for
            </li>
            <li>
              I assume full responsibility for any injuries which may occur to me, as well as the
              safety of my family and guests, and do hereby fully and forever discharge and release
              LLT, South West Catchments Council, and the SITE owner and their employees, board
              members, officers, agents, authorized volunteers, representatives, consultants,
              insurers and sureties, and their successors and assigns (collectively, the "Released
              Parties") from any "Claims.” "Claims," as used in this document, mean any and all
              claims, demands, damages, rights of action or causes of action, present or future,
              whether the same be known, anticipated or unanticipated, resulting from or arising out
              of my presence or the presence of my family members and guests at the garden,
              activities at the SITE, and/or participation in activities connected with the SITE or
              LLT including, without limitation, any of the foregoing resulting from or arising out
              of the negligence of a Released Party. Further, I hereby waive any and all Claims
              against a Released Party.
            </li>
            <li>
              I expressly acknowledge that participation in the SITE and memorial forest is for my
              purposes and not for the purpose of any one or more of the Released Parties.
            </li>
            <li>
              I understand and agree that the conservation legacy zone service is provided fully by
              South West Catchments Council, and to the extent legally permissible, I release,
              indemnify and hold LLT and the land owner harmless from any and all claims related to
              the planting and maintenance of my trees in the conservation zone except to the extent
              such claim relates directly to any damage or loss resulting from the treatment of
              ashes by LLT.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            I have read, understand and agree to the terms and responsibilities as stated in this
            document including the standard terms and conditions on page 2 of this document.
          </p>
          <p>(Or Parent/legal guardian signature if participant is under the age of 18).</p>

          <h2 id="terms-and-warranty">Living Legacy Memorial Tree terms &amp; warranty</h2>
          <p>
            CONGRATULATIONS on choosing to honour the circle of life through a Living Legacy
            memorial.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are proud to offer LIVING LEGACY TREE to retell the life stories of your loved one.
            We understand how important this event is and we want to do everything we can to ensure
            the healthy growth of your LIVING LEGACY TREE. Before you proceed, please ensure you
            understand the different options we provide; each option will involve a different level
            of care and maintenance of your LIVING LEGACY TREE. When you elect to plant your LIVING
            LEGACY TREE at one of our partner conservation parks or sanctuaries you will need to
            sign the attached waiver. Where you choose to plant your LIVING LEGACY TREE privately
            Living Legacy Pty Ltd can only provide limited warranties that relate to the
            effectiveness of our ash treatment and its suitability for native plants in healthy
            soil. Under any of these options we suggest that you retain a small amount of ash in a
            keepsake. We offer a beautiful crystal keepsake as part of your package.
          </p>

          <h2 id="cancellations-and-refunds">Cancellations &amp; Refunds</h2>
          <p>
            Cancellations made at within 21 from purchase will be fully refunded (less a 5% charge
            for administration and processing fees from third parties).
          </p>
          <p>
            Cancellations made at after 21 days but at least 21 days prior to the planting day will
            be refunded 50% of the purchase price.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cancellations made less than 21 days prior to the planting date, will not be refunded,
            except in situations of legitimate and substantiated emergency and where Living Legacy
            has agreed to provide a full refund (less the booking fee).
          </p>
          <p>
            For this project, Living Legacy will commit significant funds to the conservation and
            management of the planting day and memorial sanctuary. These funds are allocated based
            on the purchases made prior to the planting date, so we are unable to give refunds
            within the 21 day period preceding the planting date.
          </p>

          <h2 id="planted-living-legacy-trees">Planted LIVING LEGACY TREES</h2>
          <p>
            Our patented infusion process is the culmination of years of research and development
            but is simple to use. LIVING LEGACY REPRESENTATIVES can undertake the infusion process
            and you may be able to take part in the process
          </p>
          <p>
            Independent Laboratory tests resulted in 100% success rate for native trees in
            Australian soils recommended by a certified local nursery for your location.
          </p>
          <p>
            Accordingly, Living Legacy Pty Ltd guarantees the growth of native trees in healthy
            soils subject to natural attrition and force majeure.
          </p>
          <p>
            Even where all precautions are taken natural attrition rates apply for all trees for
            various reasons including but not limited to (extreme weather, flooding, disease or
            vandalism) known as “Force Majeure” and as such the Living Legacy Pty Ltd guarantee does
            not apply to damage or loss resulting from any force Majeure events.
          </p>
          <p>
            Even though the likelihood of unsuccessful infusion is extremely low, due to the
            unavoidable natural attrition rate of any tree Living Legacy Pty Ltd recommends that ALL
            customers retain a small part of the cremated remains which can be used as a contingency
            if the original tree(s) fail to grow successfully in the first instance. If a LIVING
            LEGACY TREE which is planted in accordance with the LIVING LEGACY CARE AND MAINTENANCE
            GUIDELINES fails to grow or dies within the first 5 years due to Living Legacy’s default
            but not where due to any Force Majeure event Living Legacy will replace the tree and
            re-perform infusion at no cost to you.
          </p>
          <p>
            LL agrees to carry out its services in accordance with the standards of the profession
            or practice relevant to the performance of those obligations, and exercising that degree
            of skill, care, diligence, prudence, foresight and operating practice which would
            reasonably and ordinarily be expected from a skilled and experienced person engaged in a
            similar type of undertaking as that of LL under the same or similar circumstances.
          </p>
          <p>
            The following are confirmations that you, understand the warranties provided by Living
            Legacy, by purchasing this LIVING LEGACY TREE you confirm that you have read these
            instructions and agree to the following:
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              LL does not warrant successful infusion where LL Guidelines are not followed, or where
              failure to grow is the result of environmental factors, force majeure or due to any
              mishandling or error made by Client.
            </li>
            <li>
              You acknowledge that by purchasing LIVING LEGACY TREE that you do not do so in
              reliance on any representation, warranty or other provision except as expressly
              provided herein, and any conditions, warranties or other terms implied by statute or
              common law are, to the greatest extent permissible by law, excluded from this
              agreement to the fullest extent permitted by law.
            </li>
            <li>
              You understand that except for the warranties provided in this clause, you accept full
              responsibility for your LIVING LEGACY TREE upon taking receipt of the TREE(S).
            </li>
            <li>
              You understand that you are responsible for choosing the appropriate tree, soil and
              location for the Living Legacy Tree. You are also responsible for providing security,
              care and maintenance of the tree and the site where the tree is located and with
              exception of the warranties provided herein you indemnify and hold Living Legacy
              harmless from and against any and all claims resulting from incidents occurring after
              delivery of the LIVING LEGACY TREE, or in relation to the maintenance and care of the
              tree.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Living Legacy’s sole and exclusive remedy for failed infusion or other breach of
            contract is to replace the tree(s) originally selected for infusion and re-supply the
            LIVING LEGACY TREE. You acknowledge that Living Legacy is not responsible for and will
            in no circumstances be responsible for retaining part of the ashes as a contingency if a
            new tree is to be planted under warranty.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section
      data-reveal
      class="mt-16 max-w-3xl lg:ml-[calc(12rem+4rem)]"
      aria-labelledby="terms-location-heading"
    >
      <Separator className="mb-12" />
      <p class="eyebrow">Information</p>
      <h2 id="terms-location-heading" class="section-title mt-4">Wellington Dam Memorial Forest</h2>
      <dl class="divide-bark/15 border-bark/15 mt-8 divide-y border-y text-base">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 py-3.5">
          <dt class="text-ink-soft shrink-0">Address</dt>
          <dd class="text-ink text-right">
            1 Wellington Dam Road, Worsley, Western Australia, Australia
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
